# T001U58: integral multiplier attempts, full target unresolved

The full statement is original-scope.md. All pinned source theorems are stipulated. The following deductions isolate an actual arithmetic-cycle index, not a new theorem nomination. No failure of the full target is proved.

## 1. Exact obstruction group and placewise success

Let L be the integral Hodge lattice of the fixed A in codimension r. It is a free group of finite rank, being a subgroup of torsion-free finite-rank Betti cohomology. For a good geometric reduction w define

    I_w = { gamma in L : some integral cycle on A_w represents gamma_w
                         simultaneously in all the required realizations }.

This is a subgroup: addition and negation of representing cycles work in every realization at once. Source001 cor:algebraic-specialization, using source032 thm:cm, gives L tensor Q inside the simultaneous rational cycle span. For a Z-basis gamma_1,...,gamma_t choose rational representing cycles separately, and clear their finitely many coefficients. The resulting positive D_w satisfies D_w L subset I_w. Consequently Q_w=L/I_w is a finite abelian group. Its exponent e_w is a genuine invariant of the actual cycle images; it is not the denominator of one arbitrarily chosen source construction.

The unchanged target is equivalent to finiteness of lcm_w e_w. Precisely, its integers N are those with e_w dividing N for every w. Equivalently there must be a finite set of rational primes T and finite bounds a_l such that v_l(e_w)<=a_l for all w and all l in T, while v_l(e_w)=0 outside T. Bounding valuations separately for each fixed l without controlling their support is insufficient. This is an exact reduction, not a new estimate.

A finite extension of K does not create a new difficulty: cycle existence is over geometric residue fields, and the absolute-Hodge comparison transports the invariant under the corresponding identifications. Once classes and model descend, conjugate places act by the induced lattice automorphisms. The target still requires all places; taking a finite extension cannot delete an infinite exceptional set.

## 2. Route A: track and combine CM transport denominators

Read source001 transport equations transport-rational-similitude and transport-eta-scaling and cor:cm-transport, followed by the complete algebraic-specialization proof. For each gamma,w it gives a CM auxiliary B_w, a rational Hodge class kappa_w, and b_w in Hom^0(A_w,B_w). If n_w b_w=h_w is an actual homomorphism and d_w Z_w is an integral representative of the rational CM cycle, then

    z_w = n_w^(-2r) h_w^* Z_{w,0},
    d_w n_w^(2r) gamma_w = cl(h_w^*(d_w Z_{w,0})).             (A)

The Chow pullback is integral between smooth varieties; it is defined by the graph and refined intersection, not by a flatness or separability assumption. Thus (A) remains valid if p divides n_w. One may take the lcm of these products over a Hodge basis to obtain D_w above.

The transport also has a rational normalization kappa=lambda^(-r) eta_B/[P:Q], with lambda the ratio of two rational divisor intersection numbers on the fixed special fiber. Clearing the denominator of a chosen CM cycle already accounts for that normalization. It must not be counted as a uniform bounded scalar merely because the ratio is rational. Neither the denominator of b_w, the cycle denominator, nor the normalization's numerator/denominator is bounded across places in the statements read. Source032 assembly uses rational maps on finite covers of arithmetic surfaces and scalar descent. The finiteness is for the fixed CM input, whereas B_w varies.

An actual abelian example shows why simply bounding the displayed auxiliary denominator is also the wrong necessary invariant. Take a CM elliptic curve E, r=1, gamma=[0], and any positive m. On a good special fiber use b=[1/m] in End^0(E_w), kappa=m^2[0], h=id and n=m. Formula (A) returns m^(-2) m^2[0]=[0]. The auxiliary denominator m is arbitrary, including p-powers, while e_w=1. This does not refute the target or the possibility of choosing better transports; it proves that an upper bound on every source transport denominator is not a necessary route to it.

A more promising attempted repair is to use many transports. For a fixed gamma,w, every valid transport supplies an integer D with D gamma in I_w. If transports supply D_1,...,D_s, Bezout gives gcd(D_1,...,D_s) gamma in I_w, by the corresponding signed integral combination of actual cycles. The gcd of even an infinite collection is generated by finitely many members, because its generated ideal in Z is principal. This permits denominator cancellation without controlling each individual auxiliary.

The precise missing estimate is: for a finite Hodge basis, choose transport/CM-cycle constructions so that the gcd of their multipliers divides one fixed N independent of w. Prime by prime this asks for a transport with bounded l-adic multiplier valuation, and valuation zero for all but a fixed finite set of l. Merely varying a quasi-isogeny by a rational scalar rescales kappa oppositely, as the elliptic example demonstrates; it creates no new cycle-index saving. No independence of these denominators is in the CM special-point or rational cycle-span contracts. I have not proved the needed avoidance estimate. This route stops at this exact arithmetic operation.

## 3. Route B: local saturation and the residue-characteristic gap

The intrinsic groups Q_w make an attempted adelic repair exact. Tensoring

    0 -> I_w -> L -> Q_w -> 0

with Z_l preserves exactness (Z_l is torsion-free, hence flat, over Z). For gamma in L, its image in Q_w tensor Z_l vanishes exactly when its class has trivial l-primary component. Hence a single integer N kills every Q_w if and only if it kills every completed quotient at every pair (w,l). Testing only l different from the residue characteristic p(w) proves at most that the remaining obstruction is p(w)-primary. The exponent of that remaining part is not controlled, and its prime support changes with w.

This point is particularly relevant to the desired simultaneous cycle: crystalline rational equality has inverted p. It cannot by itself remove a p-primary cycle-index obstruction. The rational source equality also cannot turn arbitrary independent Z_l-linear combinations of cycle classes into one Z-linear cycle. A genuine local-to-global repair must control the *integral cycle lattice* I_w, not merely prove integrality of the cohomology tensor. Once its completed quotients vanish at every prime, the finite-group argument above does give one integral cycle; before that it does not.

The distinction is not a counterexample invented against source truth. Rational cycle span and integral cycle saturation are different even for actual abelian varieties; the primary integral-Fourier work treats the latter as an extra hypothesis. Its one-cycle Fourier operation uses algebraicity of a specified divided Poincare class, and has bounded factorial denominators in that codimension. Its statement is not an all-codimension integral lift for arbitrary CM Hodge classes. Milne's 2025 integral-Tate note concerns finitely generated characteristic-zero fields, not a finite-field counterexample to this target. No such counterexample is claimed.

For generic algebraic Hodge classes there is a paid solution: choose integral multiples of a finite generic cycle basis, spread their closures through the abelian scheme, and specialize. One common multiple works for every good geometric fiber, with integral specialization at every characteristic and all cycle-class compatibilities. The CM case is therefore already paid by source032 plus this elementary spreading step. This does not handle a general fixed A with Hodge classes not known to be algebraic on its generic fiber. Promoting the CM case would weaken the frozen target and is excluded.

## 4. Route C: why a common finite family would be much stronger

One possible attempt to replace the unbounded collection of placewise cycles by a finite construction is to parameterize them by one finite collection of projective, flat families of cycles on the fixed abelian scheme. There is a precise obstruction to treating that as automatic compactness.

Suppose for one fixed gamma and positive N there is such a finite collection T_j -> S, with cycle classes in the pulled-back smooth proper cohomology, and that their geometric fibers provide representatives of N gamma at infinitely many places. After finite extension of K, the absolute-Hodge class is Galois invariant and is a section of the rational l-adic local system away from l. Decompose the finite-type parameter spaces into finitely many connected pieces on which the relative cycle class is defined. On a connected piece, equality between the cycle section and the pulled-back section N gamma is all-or-nothing: two sections of a locally constant sheaf agreeing at a geometric point agree everywhere. Components supported at closed places account for only finitely many places. Thus one matching component dominates S. Its characteristic-zero fiber has an algebraic point over Qbar; the cycle there has l-adic class N gamma, and comparison gives Betti class N gamma. In particular gamma is generically rationally algebraic.

The argument requires actual finite-type parameter spaces and relative cycle sections; it is not an assertion that an arbitrary collection of integral Chow classes has those bounded data. Passing to all Hilbert/Chow components destroys that finiteness. The source specialization proof chooses a Hilbert component separately for each CM auxiliary. It supplies neither a common auxiliary nor bounded cycle complexity on A_w. Therefore this compactness route, if it paid arbitrary Hodge classes, would in fact yield the rational Hodge conjecture for A itself. The uniform-multiplier target imposes no complexity bound and does not imply that conclusion by this argument. I have not proved a finite-family replacement or a bound on e_w.

## Disposition

T001U58 remains unresolved in its entire frozen scope. The useful conclusions are the intrinsic finite quotient, the exact gcd opportunity, the uncontrolled residue-characteristic component, and the stronger conclusion required by the finite-family route. Their proofs are elementary arithmetic/cycle bookkeeping around the source interfaces, not a substantial theorem. No narrower statement is nominated. A meaningful continuation would need an actual integral denominator-avoidance construction for varying CM transports, or a uniform bound on the completed integral cycle-index quotients including l=p. Repeating rational algebraicity or finite-basis clearing does not advance that operation.
